--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/decisions/0001-stable-task-ids.md
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# ADR 0001: Stable task identifiers
+
+## Context
+
+The task list used titles as both identity and lookup keys. Renaming a task therefore changed how callers had to refer to it. The feature requirement is to give every task a unique identifier that remains usable after renaming.
+
+## Decision
+
+Each list assigns string IDs in add order (`task-1`, `task-2`, ...). The task map is keyed by ID, while title uniqueness remains an independent list invariant. The public list operations accept IDs, and `get(id)` retrieves a task by ID.
+
+## Consequences
+
+IDs are stable across task updates and deterministic without reading the clock or using randomness. IDs are unique within one list; separate lists can assign the same IDs. Title duplicate checks scan the list because title is no longer the storage key.
+
+## Requirement
+
+Implement stable, unique per-list task identifiers and ID-based access and operations.
